Enhancement: command-parity batch (merge, repoinfo, retention, dump)

Vaultic now provides `merge`, an append-only snapshot-tree union command that
creates a new snapshot without modifying its source snapshots or repository
objects. Conflicting paths use the newest source; source snapshot IDs are kept
in additive `merged_snapshots` metadata.

`repoinfo` provides read-only object counts and stored sizes for packs, keys,
snapshots, and indexes, including JSON output. It is compatible with lock-free
read operation.

`forget` gains minutely, quarterly-yearly, half-yearly, and matching
`--keep-within-*` retention periods; `--keep-none` aliases the existing
explicit all-removal acknowledgement. `dump` supports `tar.gz` and target
extension based `auto` archive format selection. `diff` accepts `latest` and
`latest~N`; `completions` aliases `generate`.

WebDAV is intentionally out of scope for this batch and remains unimplemented.

